       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, which is 16,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the usual limit for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision (800 mg four times daily). Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day. This order is 5 times the prescription maximum.\n- **Risks at that dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain.\n- **600 mg** PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **800 mg** PO three or four times daily (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it. I'd also confirm it with your resident or attending. If you want a specific dose, it would help to add an indication, a \"with food\" instruction, or a duration to the order note."
